My machine setup. One command:

```sh
git clone https://github.com/julianbonilla/dotfiles.git ~/dotfiles
~/dotfiles/bootstrap.sh
```

`bootstrap.sh` (idempotent — safe to re-run) installs Homebrew, runs
`brew bundle`, symlinks the configs, sets fish as the default shell, and
installs fisher plus the tide prompt (plugins are declared in
`.config/fish/fish_plugins`).

Afterwards: open a new terminal and run `tide configure` — or copy
`~/.config/fish/fish_variables` from another machine for the identical
prompt.
